            <ArticleTitle>Stent embolization during intracoronary stenting.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>833-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Nine patients with systemic embolization complicating intracoronary stenting (incidence 1.8%) are described. Although this rare complication was not associated with any clinical sequelae, great care should be taken to prevent this possibility, especially in patients with unfavorable anatomic characteristics, including lesions in the left circumflex artery, at bend points, and calcified lesions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
